net: preserve SKBFL_SHARED_FRAG when skb_zerocopy() references frags

skb_zerocopy() attaches the source skb's page frags by reference
(nfnetlink_queue COPY_PACKET and other callers), but unlike every other
frag-referencing helper (__pskb_copy_fclone(), skb_split(), GSO, GRO,
tcp_fragment(), xfrm_iptfs) it does not carry SKBFL_SHARED_FRAG over to
the destination skb.  Pages spliced from the page cache thus arrive in a
new skb with no annotation, and consumers that must not write them in
place (esp4/esp6 input, checksum helpers) cannot detect them.

Propagate the annotation while the frags are referenced.

Also make esp4/esp6 output avoid in-place encryption when the skb
carries shared frags, closing the same in-place write from the
encryption side (splice() -> UDP -> xfrm policy).  The shared case uses
the existing copied-trailer path -- which materialises references and
clears SKBFL_MANAGED_FRAG_REFS -- or skb_cow_data() when the frag array
cannot take the trailer; both leave the payload private before crypto
writes it.

No cost on normal paths: one flag word update on the zerocopy builders,
and one extra shinfo test on the ESP output fast path.

diff --git a/net/core/skbuff.c b/net/core/skbuff.c
index eb9fcc4..a6bd991 100644
--- a/net/core/skbuff.c
+++ b/net/core/skbuff.c
@@ -3966,6 +3966,14 @@ skb_zerocopy(struct sk_buff *to, struct sk_buff *from, int len, int hlen)
 	}
 	skb_shinfo(to)->nr_frags = j;
 
+	/* The frags were taken by reference, so they may point into the page
+	 * cache (sendfile()/splice()) or into memory the producer cannot
+	 * write.  Carry the annotation over so that in-place writers copy
+	 * instead of corrupting the backing pages.
+	 */
+	if (j)
+		skb_shinfo(to)->flags |= skb_shinfo(from)->flags & SKBFL_SHARED_FRAG;
+
 	if (i > 0 && from->unreadable)
 		to->unreadable = 1;
 
diff --git a/net/ipv4/esp4.c b/net/ipv4/esp4.c
index ae70156..ed279d3 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/esp4.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/esp4.c
@@ -427,14 +427,20 @@ int esp_output_head(struct xfrm_state *x, struct sk_buff *skb, struct esp_info *
 		goto cow;
 
 	if (!skb_cloned(skb)) {
-		if (tailen <= skb_tailroom(skb)) {
+		/* In-place encryption must not write into frags that belong
+		 * to the page cache (sendfile()/splice()) or to memory the
+		 * sender cannot write; use a copying path instead.
+		 */
+		if (tailen <= skb_tailroom(skb) &&
+		    !skb_has_shared_frag(skb)) {
 			nfrags = 1;
 			trailer = skb;
 			tail = skb_tail_pointer(trailer);
 
 			goto skip_cow;
-		} else if ((skb_shinfo(skb)->nr_frags < MAX_SKB_FRAGS)
-			   && !skb_has_frag_list(skb)) {
+		}
+		if ((skb_shinfo(skb)->nr_frags < MAX_SKB_FRAGS) &&
+		    !skb_has_frag_list(skb)) {
 			int allocsize;
 			struct sock *sk = skb->sk;
 			struct page_frag *pfrag = &x->xfrag;
